Oil paintings are artworks created using pigments mixed with oil-based binders, commonly applied to canvas, wood panels, or other suitable surfaces. This medium is known for its rich colors, smooth blending capabilities, and ability to create detailed textures and layered effects. Artists can use different application techniques to achieve a wide range of finishes, from thin transparent layers to thick, textured brushstrokes.
